<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  RBM troop perks: hero perks for regular (non-hero) troops.

  Format
    <TroopPerks>
      <Troop id="troop_string_id">        the troop's id, as in spnpccharacters.xml (e.g. vlandian_sharpshooter)
        <Perk id="PerkStringId"/>          one per perk; any number
      </Troop>
    </TroopPerks>

  Perk ids are the perk's StringId: the skill name followed by the perk name, no spaces, as in vanilla's
  DefaultPerks (e.g. CrossbowSteady, CrossbowWindWinder, BowRapidFire, BowMountedArchery, RidingSagittarius,
  OneHandedShieldBearer, AthleticsIgnorePain, PolearmFootwork, TwoHandedStrongGrip). War Sails perks use their
  own ids (e.g. ShipwrightsInsight). The perk icon files in SandBox/GUI/SandBoxSpriteData.xml (SPPerks\<id>) list
  them all.

  How it works
    - A listed perk counts as owned by that troop in battle, with its normal vanilla effect. Nothing on the
      campaign map changes. Needs RBM Combat and the Troop Perks setting (RBM Configuration > Combat).
    - Only PERSONAL perk effects do anything: a troop is never a captain, party leader, quartermaster or
      governor, so the captain/party/leader halves of a perk are ignored. A perk with no personal effect at
      all does nothing.
    - Entries are not inherited along the upgrade tree: list each troop that should have a perk.
    - Heroes (lords, companions, the player) are ignored; they have their own perks.
    - The troop's perks are listed in its tooltip and on its encyclopedia page.
    - Unknown troop or perk ids are skipped and reported in the game log (rgl_log), as are perks below.
    - Other modules can ship their own ModuleData/rbm_troop_perks.xml; all active modules' files are merged.

  Perks that do NOT work for troops (troop-perk audit, v1.5.4; full list with reasons in
  tools/TroopPerkEditor/audit/README.md of the RBM repository):
    Hero or player only (never checked for a troop): BowHorseMaster, CrossbowMountedCrossbowman,
      TwoHandedProjectileDeflection, TwoHandedBaptisedInBlood, ThrowingRunningThrow, BowEagleEye,
      ThrowingFocus, CrossbowLongShots, RidingWellStraped, AthleticsDurable, AthleticsSteady, AthleticsStrong,
      VigorousSmith, StrongSmith, EnduringSmith, WeaponMasterSmith, MedicineMinisterOfHealth,
      ShipwrightsInsight (War Sails).
    Campaign only (map, trade, persuasion, smithing, post-battle healing): every personal Charm and Trade
      perk, the smithing-screen Smithing perks (all but CraftingSharpenedEdge/SharpenedTip), and the
      off-battlefield personal perks of Roguery, Leadership, Medicine, Tactics and Athletics (e.g.
      RogueryScarface, LeadershipPresence, MedicineWalkItOff, TacticsBesieged, AthleticsStamina), plus Arr
      and Resilience (War Sails).
    Removed by RBM for everyone: OneHandedArrowCatcher (RBM fixes the shield's missile catch size).
    Perks with no personal effect at all (captain, party leader, governor, ... only) also do nothing.
  AthleticsMightyBlow is only given to a troop with Athletics above 250 (skipped otherwise, and logged): its HP
  bonus is (Athletics skill - 250), so below that a troop would lose hit points.

  Example (not active):
    <Troop id="vlandian_sharpshooter">
      <Perk id="CrossbowSteady"/>
      <Perk id="CrossbowWindWinder"/>
    </Troop>
-->
